<title>DENMARK: NIB raises four-percent, six-year bond offer.</title>
<headline>NIB raises four-percent, six-year bond offer.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nordic Investment Bank (NIB) on Tuesday raised an existing 500 million crown, four-percent, six-year bond offer to 700 million crowns, lead manager Gudme Raaschou Bankaktieselskab said in a statement distributed by the Copenhagen Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>All the bonds, which mature in 2002, were sold, it said.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
